<ArticleLayout title="About Child Savings Lab" description="An independent, source-linked tool platform for families navigating children’s savings accounts and financial choices.">
  <h2>Why this exists</h2>
  <p>New account rules often arrive as forms, notices, and dense guidance. Child Savings Lab turns those materials into transparent tools while keeping the source close to the answer.</p>
  <h2>Why the name is broader than Trump Accounts</h2>
  <p>Trump Accounts are the first search and product cluster, not the permanent boundary of the brand. The platform is designed to expand to 529 plans, UGMA/UTMA, Custodial Roth IRAs, ABLE accounts, children’s investing, and employer benefits.</p>
  <h2>What we are not</h2>
  <p>We are not a government website, investment adviser, tax preparer, law firm, or official partner of the Trump Accounts program. We do not claim professional review that has not occurred.</p>
  <h2>How trust is built</h2>
  <p>Important claims link to primary sources. Rules carry verification dates. Calculator assumptions are visible. Corrections update logic and tests—not only page copy.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
